From 195ed0d97444fcf6b945b96bf0842e3bc38a51cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSI M2: LAPIC MSI message-delivery core

msi_deliver(m, addr, data) in src/lapic.c decodes one x86 MSI/MSI-X
message and lands it on lapic_set_irr_dest -- the exact sink the
IOAPIC already proves, so PPR arbitration, intack and EOI behave
identically for both interrupt transports.

Decode/measurement summary (all pinned by the new tests/test_msi.c
lane, observed through deliverable -> intack -> EOI):
- physical Fixed delivers as addressed; an unroutable destination id
  falls back to the BSP (the IOAPIC's documented rule);
- Lowest Priority degenerates to Fixed at the named destination --
  there is no arbitration fabric to consult (RH only steers that
  arbitration, so it is decoded and set aside);
- flat logical destinations match LDR[31:24], first claimant wins,
  unclaimed falls back to the BSP;
- a vector below 16 latches ESR receive-illegal-vector and pends
  nothing; a non-APIC address is ignored entirely;
- level/trigger bits are advisory: a message is an edge by
  construction, the source keeps its pending state (MSI_PLAN 2);
- SMI/NMI/INIT/ExtINT and reserved delivery modes are logged and
  dropped -- never fabricated into injections this core cannot honor.

The lane is wired into make test / make test-sanitize / .PHONY /
clean.  NC: msi_deliver stubbed -> 9 failures.  Gates: make test,
make test-sanitize, both SeaBIOS ISO lanes green.  Nothing calls
msi_deliver yet; device routing is M3.
